# Wallpaper manifest — the desktop wallpaper is IN the repo (it is small, and it
# is the source of the whole colour palette, so losing it would lose the look).
# Format: file | source | resolution | licence/notes
#
# Changing the wallpaper is a two-step change, in this order:
#   1. drop the new image in this directory and point palette.toml at it
#   2. bash scripts/desktop/gen-palette.sh   (regenerates every colour artefact)
#   3. bash scripts/desktop/15-palette.sh && bash scripts/desktop/60-wallpaper.sh
firewatch-dusk.jpg | https://wallhaven.cc/w/mdjrqy | 5120x2880 | wallhaven SFW/general; personal use. Firewatch-style dusk ridge line; the orange sun is the palette's source colour (#e8931c, forced in palette.toml — the automatic pick was the forest green).
